<description><![CDATA[Dalmia Bharat, India's fourth-largest cement manufacturer, will hold a board meeting on November 23. The meeting will focus on a proposal for a buyback of fully paid-up equity shares. Specific details regarding the buyback size, price, and number of shares have not been disclosed yet. The company also plans to expand its cement capacity to 75 million tonnes per annum by FY28.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/dalmia-bharat-to-consider-share-buyback-at-nov-23-board-meeting/articleshow/135966836.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135966836,imgsize-16550.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/dalmia-bharat-to-consider-share-buyback-at-nov-23-board-meeting/articleshow/135966836.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:58:41 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[PSBs' net profit rises 17% to Rs 1.10 lakh cr in H1 FY27; business crosses Rs 300 lakh crore]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Public sector banks in India have reported a remarkable 16.9 percent rise in net profits during the first half of this fiscal year, reflecting a thriving financial environment. With total business reaching Rs 301.6 lakh crore, and a notable drop in the gross non-performing assets ratio to an unprecedented 1.69 percent, the banks are demonstrating improved stability.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/psbs-net-profit-rises-17-to-rs-1-10-lakh-cr-in-h1-fy27-business-crosses-rs-300-lakh-crore/articleshow/135965650.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135965650,imgsize-264927.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/psbs-net-profit-rises-17-to-rs-1-10-lakh-cr-in-h1-fy27-business-crosses-rs-300-lakh-crore/articleshow/135965650.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:52:28 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kotak MF, BlackRock, others buy stake worth Rs 1,905 cr in Groww]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Kotak Mahindra Mutual Fund (MF) led the buying spree, acquiring 2.05 crore shares or a 0.33 per cent stake, for Rs 448.95 crore, making it the biggest buyer in the transaction.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/kotak-mf-blackrock-others-buy-stake-worth-rs-1905-cr-in-groww/articleshow/135964570.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135964570,imgsize-49176.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/kotak-mf-blackrock-others-buy-stake-worth-rs-1905-cr-in-groww/articleshow/135964570.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:52:43 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[PI Industries among 5 stocks hitting 52-week low; slipped up to 26% in a month]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Five BSE 500 stocks, including PI Industries, Aditya Birla Fashion and Retail and Thermax, hit fresh 52-week lows as the market weakened, with losses reaching 26% in a month.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/pi-industries-among-5-stocks-hitting-52-week-low-slipped-up-to-26-in-a-month/slideshow/135961979.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135961798,imgsize-47968.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/pi-industries-among-5-stocks-hitting-52-week-low-slipped-up-to-26-in-a-month/slideshow/135961979.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:01:06 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[SpiceJet board approves up to Rs 5,500 crore fundraise amid operational challenges; stock hits 5% upper circuit]]> </title><description><![CDATA[SpiceJet's board of directors announced a fundraising plan to raise up to Rs 5,500 crore. The airline's shares have surged significantly, hitting the upper circuit for six consecutive sessions. Flight cancellations and operational disruptions have caused significant challenges for SpiceJet in recent days. The airline is focusing on rebuilding capacity and ensuring operational reliability going forward. The fundraising aims to strengthen its financial position and support fleet expansion efforts.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/spicejet-board-approves-up-to-rs-5500-crore-fundraise-to-support-fleet-expansion-drive-revival/articleshow/135958224.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135958224,imgsize-145066.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/spicejet-board-approves-up-to-rs-5500-crore-fundraise-to-support-fleet-expansion-drive-revival/articleshow/135958224.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:10:01 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Govt weighs tax tweaks to boost stock trading, curb derivatives: Report]]> </title><description><![CDATA[The government is reviewing proposals to cut securities transaction tax on cash equities by 50% while raising levies on derivatives to curb speculative trading and encourage broader market participation. Officials are also considering a reduction in long-term capital gains tax. The recommendations will be presented to Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman ahead of Budget 2027.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/govt-weighs-tax-tweaks-to-boost-stock-trading-curb-derivatives/articleshow/135953824.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135953824,imgsize-183608.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/govt-weighs-tax-tweaks-to-boost-stock-trading-curb-derivatives/articleshow/135953824.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:54:58 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[How Ashish Kacholia, Radhakishan Damani, Madhusudan Kela and other ace investors reshuffled their portfolios in Q2]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Mukul Agrawal, Akash Bhanshali and Ashish Kacholia emerge as the biggest portfolio gainers among prominent individual investors in the September quarter. Meanwhile, Radhakishan Damani records the steepest decline. The analysis examines their portfolio values, top stock holdings and changes in shareholding across listed companies.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/how-ashish-kacholia-radhakishan-damani-madhusudan-kela-and-other-ace-investors-reshuffled-their-portfolios-in-q2/slideshow/135953760.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135953460,imgsize-33648.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/how-ashish-kacholia-radhakishan-damani-madhusudan-kela-and-other-ace-investors-reshuffled-their-portfolios-in-q2/slideshow/135953760.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:39:19 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[16 microcap stocks surge up to 390% in CY26, emerge as multibaggers]]> </title><description><![CDATA[The Nifty Microcap 250 has outperformed the benchmark Nifty 50 in CY26, with several constituents delivering multibagger returns. Sixteen microcap stocks have more than doubled investors' wealth so far this year, led by Sigma Advanced Systems, while nearly 50 stocks in the index have gained over 50%.]]> </description><link>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/16-microcap-stocks-surge-up-to-390-in-cy26-emerge-as-multibaggers/slideshow/135953025.cms</link><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://img.etimg.com/photo/msid-135952551,imgsize-5134.cms" length="0"/><guid>https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/stocks/news/16-microcap-stocks-surge-up-to-390-in-cy26-emerge-as-multibaggers/slideshow/135953025.cms</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:14:42 +0530</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Max Healthcare among 10 Nifty stocks rallied up to 22% in 1 month. Did you miss the rally?]]> </title><description><![CDATA[Nift